examples.question_text:
A report claims: “Pool visits increased every month.” Check the claim against the graph and write a supported alternative.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=0.01cm]
\path[use as bounding box] (-1.8,-90) rectangle (4.9,450);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(4.8,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,440);
\foreach \v in {0,100,200,300,400} {\draw[black] (-0.08,\v)--(0,\v); \path (-0.12,\v) node[left,text=black,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\foreach \x/\month/\count in {1/Jan/240,2/Feb/360,3/Mar/300,4/Apr/400} {\draw[black] (\x-0.3,0) rectangle (\x+0.3,\count); \path (\x,0) node[below,text=black,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {\month};}
\path (-1.5,220) node[rotate=90,text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {Visits};
\path (2.5,-65) node[text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont] {Month};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
